     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p24-definition-block",
     "replacement": "A **perfect square trinomial** is a trinomial that is the expansion of $(a+b)^2$ or $(a-b)^2$.\n\nIt has the form $a^2\\pm2ab+b^2$.\n\n1. Find the square roots of the first term, $\\sqrt{a^2}=a$, and the last term, $\\sqrt{b^2}=b$.\n2. Check that the middle term is $2ab$ or $-2ab$.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p24-definition-block",
     "targetFingerprint": "25f410de3126700a3c98399248b670d152ea514e0d89644131636f0783c63b36",
