   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p49-definition",
     "replacement": "A **quadratic trinomial** has the form $ax^2+bx+c$, where $a$, $b$ and $c$ are non-zero numbers. It is **non-monic** when the coefficient of $x^2$ is not $1$, that is, when $a\\ne1$.\n\nTo factorise a non-monic quadratic trinomial: $ax^2+bx+c$\n\n1. Identify the product: $ac$\n2. Identify the sum: $b$\n3. Find a factor pair, $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, that has product $ac$ and sum $b$.\n4. Split $bx$ into $\\alpha x+\\beta x$.\n5. Factorise by grouping in pairs.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p49-definition",
